?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Denaʼina Civic and Convention Center","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.215,"lo":-149.894,"d":463,"ds":"The Dena'ina Civic and Convention Center is a convention center in downtown Anchorage, Alaska, United States. The $111 million, 200,000-square-foot (19,000 m2) facility opened in September 2008. The Denaʼina Center increased Anchorage's civic and convention capacity by 300 percent.","wpu":"Denaʼina Civic and Convention Center","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Dena%27ina_Civic_and_Convention_Center._Anchorage%2C_Alaska.jpg/960px-Dena%27ina_Civic_and_Convention_Center._Anchorage%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Delaney Park Strip","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.213333,"lo":-149.901667,"d":526,"ds":"The Delaney Park Strip is an 11-block park in the Municipality of Anchorage, Alaska. Originally a firebreak, the Park Strip would become Anchorage's first airfield.","wpu":"Delaney Park Strip","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Alaskan_Veterans_Memorial_at_Delaney_Park_Strip._%2847708962232%29.jpg/960px-Alaskan_Veterans_Memorial_at_Delaney_Park_Strip._%2847708962232%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Archdiocese of Anchorage–Juneau","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.219722,"lo":-149.878889,"d":1146,"ds":"The Archdiocese of Anchorage–Juneau (Latin: Archidiœcesis Ancoragiensis–Junellensis) is an archdiocese of the Roman Catholic Church in southern Alaska in the United States. The archdiocese has a single suffragan diocese, the Diocese of Fairbanks. The mother church cathedral of the archdiocese is Our Lady of Guadalupe Cathedral in Anchorage.","wpu":"Archdiocese of Anchorage–Juneau","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe_Cathedral_%28Anchorage%2C_Alaska%29_2024_-_cropped.jpg/960px-Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe_Cathedral_%28Anchorage%2C_Alaska%29_2024_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"McKinley Tower Apartments","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.218889,"lo":-149.8775,"d":1208,"ds":"The McKinley Tower Apartments, previously known as the East 4th & Denali Apartments, the Mt. McKinley Building, the McKay (or MacKay) Building and the McKinley Building, is a historic apartment building at 337 East Fourth Avenue in the eastern downtown of Anchorage, Alaska. Originally constructed by Swalling Construction owners, John H.","wpu":"McKinley Tower Apartments","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/McKinley_Tower_Apartments_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Anchorage Memorial Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.215,"lo":-149.876111,"d":1321,"ds":"The Anchorage Memorial Park, also known as Anchorage Cemetery, is a 22-acre (89,000 m2) cemetery located in Anchorage, Alaska, United States. Covering nine city blocks, the cemetery separates the city's downtown and Fairview neighborhoods.","wpu":"Anchorage Memorial Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Anchorage_Memorial_Park_Cemetery.jpg/960px-Anchorage_Memorial_Park_Cemetery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Greater Friendship Baptist Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.2099,"lo":-149.8665,"d":2007,"ds":"Greater Friendship Baptist Church is a Baptist church in Anchorage, Alaska. It is affiliated with the Southern Baptist Convention. The church property was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2019.","wpu":"Greater Friendship Baptist Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/AK_Anchorage_Greater_Friendship_Baptist_Church_0004.tif/lossless-page1-960px-AK_Anchorage_Greater_Friendship_Baptist_Church_0004.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Cathedral of Our Lady of Guadalupe (Alaska)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.184928,"lo":-149.944044,"d":4369,"ds":"Cathedral of Our Lady of Guadalupe of the Catholic Church is located in Anchorage, Alaska, United States. It is the cathedral and a parish church of the Archdiocese of Anchorage–Juneau. Our Lady of Guadalupe is the seat of the archbishop along with the Co-Cathedral of the Nativity of the Blessed Virgin Mary, in Juneau.","wpu":"Cathedral of Our Lady of Guadalupe (Alaska)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe_Cathedral_%28Anchorage%2C_Alaska%29_2024.jpg/960px-Our_Lady_of_Guadalupe_Cathedral_%28Anchorage%2C_Alaska%29_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"UAA/APU Consortium Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":61.190556,"lo":-149.8175,"d":5370,"ds":"The UAA/APU Consortium Library (Consortium Library) is a joint library serving the University of Alaska Anchorage and Alaska Pacific University, established in 1973 and refurbished in 2004. According to self-reported statistics from 2016, the library has approximately 728,000 volumes on site and averages 12,000 visitors per week during the academic year.","wpu":"UAA/APU Consortium Library","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Consortium_Library_University_of_Alaska_Anchorage.jpg/960px-Consortium_Library_University_of_Alaska_Anchorage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Anchorage (Denaʼina: Dgheyay Kaq'; Dgheyaytnu), officially the Municipality of Anchorage, is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Alaska. With a population of 291,247 at the 2020 census, it contains nearly 40 percent of the state's population. The Anchorage metropolitan area, which includes Anchorage and the neighboring Matanuska-Susitna Borough, had a population of 398,328 in 2020, accounting for more than half the state's population.","wpu":"Anchorage, Alaska","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Anchorage%2C_Alaska_skyline.jpg/960px-Anchorage%2C_Alaska_skyline.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}